# Reified RSpaces — Formal Verification (P1: the storage substrate, P2: the
# wire encoding, P4: the hashmap:queue slice, its metering and its legacy
# charges, P5 wave W2: the engine, the bag, cell and stack disciplines, the
# Array and Vector stores, the PathMap paths and the P5 families, P5 wave
# W3: the joins of one space and the PathMap engine, P6: the exact
# similarity decisions of the VectorDB family, P7: the theory seam, P8: the
# translation of receives on spaces that user agents implement, P10: the
# checkpoint model of the host)
#
# Mechanizes the P1 headlines of the Reified RSpaces campaign for the
# SpaceTxnHost / SpaceStoreHandle / SpaceTxn substrate in rspace++. The
# design is p1-design-report §1-§3 and §5(a) (plan decision 19, D1-D7).
#
#   EventCorrelation  H1-H12: commit parity with the host (observer calls,
#                     events, status and store), counter timing, replay
#                     pairing, view coherence, joins lockstep, sub-orders,
#                     abort, event coverage, peeks, reporting.
#                     H17, H19-H21 (P1 fix rules): canonical groups fail
#                     closed, replay directives fail closed, one
#                     transaction per parent order, store identity. Round 2:
#                     a canonical group is non-decreasing and can repeat a
#                     channel (FR-1'), and the parent tracker resets per
#                     evaluation scope, on a store swap and on a session
#                     change (FR-5'). Round 3: a produce-side peek fire
#                     never stores its incoming datum, and the agent
#                     re-offers it as the next operation (FR-10).
#                     Decision 45 (Rule E): a peek fire removes its stored
#                     non-persistent records as the host does, and the
#                     agent stores them again. So the commit equals the
#                     host program whose reducer sends the peeked data
#                     again (H11, peek_reproduces_trace_eq_host). H23
#                     (decision 36): replay reproduces the run of play.
#   VolatileSweep     H13-H16: exact sweep, absent delete, root neutrality,
#                     leaf record count. H18, H22 (P1 fix rules): canonical
#                     reads are root neutral, the checkpoint rejects two
#                     actions on one key. Round 2: the sorted list is the
#                     unique canonical member of its permutation class
#                     (FR-1'), and the sweep through the handle fails closed
#                     under an open transaction of the same task (FR-9').
#   Encoding          P2: the 12 headlines of the marker-tuple encoding of
#                     the Reified RSpaces syntax (p2-design-report §5), and
#                     3 headlines of plan revision I-20: the hooks recompute
#                     the derived connective_used flags before the strict
#                     decode. Retired from the gate by decision 112, and the
#                     file stays on disk as the frozen evidence of the marker
#                     encoding.
#   SyntaxFields      Decision 112 (15 headlines): the Reified syntax as
#                     protobuf fields. The field numbers, the decoders against
#                     the encoders, the canonical named params, one carrier
#                     per construct, the former marker tuples as ordinary
#                     tuples, the term schedule, substitution, the proto3 and
#                     bincode forms of a term without the new fields, and the
#                     derived flags that no decoder reads.
#   Namespace         P4 (11 headlines): the 0xE0 ids of the native spaces,
#                     their decoder, and the canonical key of a channel.
#   RecordEnvelope    P4 (8 headlines): the record envelopes D, K, S and C
#                     (plan revision M-2) and the config record (I-17).
#   CounterConflict   P4 (9 headlines): every queue operation bumps a
#                     counter, so HEAD's merge check #1 sees cross-branch
#                     races (plan revision M-1). A merge without a race is
#                     a serial run.
#   HeadOnlyDisciplines
#                     P4 (9 headlines): the head-only queue discipline and
#                     the produce and consume plans of GenericSpace.
#   SpaceRefs         P4 (11 headlines): space references, channel routing
#                     R1-R7, the USE wrapper, the handle dispatch and the
#                     native fail-closed rule (decision 46). P5 (1
#                     headline): a receive query routes its inner channel.
#   SpaceFactory      P4 (8 headlines): the space families, the factory
#                     constructor, the space id, persistent sends to system
#                     ops and SpaceAlreadyExists. P5 (5 headlines): the
#                     registered families follow the dispatch arms, the
#                     FIPS alias, and the constructor params (F7, F26-F28,
#                     I-10).
#   AgentReadCoverage Removed by decision 96 (decision 89): DR-131 of
#                     feature/cost-accounted-rho removes the host-work
#                     metering and its theories, so this module goes with
#                     the metering of decision 42. Restore it with git show
#                     6bf10a721:formal/rocq/reified_rspaces/theories/AgentReadCoverage.v.
#                     It was: Decision 42 (8 headlines): a space agent
#                     reserves each read and copy before it makes it (DR-88
#                     of feature/cost-accounted-rho), its reservations
#                     precede the commit, and its charges do not depend on
#                     the list order of the staged view or on unread
#                     payloads. P5 (1 headline): the staging primitives of
#                     the S1 engine reserve before they read or grow.
#   LegacyCharges     Removed by decision 90 (decision 69): DR-134 of
#                     feature/cost-accounted-rho deletes the legacy meter,
#                     so the merge of 702496775 removes Option P and this
#                     module. Restore it with git show
#                     6bf10a721:formal/rocq/reified_rspaces/theories/LegacyCharges.v.
#                     It was: Decision 45, Option P (2 headlines): the legacy
#                     storage charges of a space transaction. The callbacks
#                     with the carried post-charges, and then the tail, make
#                     the charges of the host program, with the same
#                     budget, stop point and applied operations (Q79).
#                     Replay with the operations of play stops where play
#                     stops (Q80).
#   CellDiscipline    P5 (3 headlines): a cell holds one record and one
#                     waiter (F15), its peek re-store never meets a full
#                     slot, and a re-entered element acts as a fresh one.
#   DataCollection    P5a (7 headlines): the bag order, the first spatial
#                     match, the multiset laws, the peek re-store as the
#                     host's second send (Rule E), and the scan metering.
#   ContinuationCollection
#                     P5a (5 headlines): waiters are removed by identity,
#                     parked once, visited in canonical order, and a head
#                     side offers one candidate.
#   Match             P5 (3 headlines): the plans use the injected matcher,
#                     check the guard as the host does, and the legacy
#                     wildcard matcher breaks pattern enforcement.
#   GenericRSpace     P5 (5 headlines): fires bind only matching entries,
#                     no match stays pending, the peek re-store equals the
#                     host's second send, and re-issues keep identities.
#   OuterStorage      P5d (8 headlines): the Array and Vector allocator, its
#                     index names, the key check (F8) and its metering.
#   VectorStore       P5d (3 headlines): the Vector store grows without a
#                     bound and keeps its indices.
#   HashMapStore      P5d (2 headlines): the HashMap store keys a collection
#                     by its canonical channel (A5). P7 step 3 (1
#                     headline): the HashSet store takes units only
#                     (HS-2, HS-3).
#   PathMapPrefix     P5e (6 headlines): path keys order paths by prefix,
#                     the re-rooting laws, the FIPS example, and a total
#                     candidate order. Wave W3 (11 headlines): the marker
#                     record and the vehicle, the path rules, single-channel
#                     deliveries and retires, the prefix contact, the second
#                     send of a peek (Rule E), no pending match, the marker
#                     invariant, the heads and their cascade, the token
#                     orders, and the metering of the prefix scan.
#   StackDiscipline   P5b (13 headlines): the head of a stack, LIFO order,
#                     head blocking, the settle loop and its termination,
#                     re-entry at the LIFO place, and one fire count for
#                     each transaction (decision 49).
#   SetDiscipline     P5a (8 headlines): the F5 set key is injective, the
#                     view keeps one representative per class, a consume
#                     retires its class over [D; n], the retire COMMs meet
#                     the staging rules, a produce-side fire retires the
#                     stored class (decision 37), a peek restores only the
#                     representative (Rule E), membership compares full keys
#                     on equal hashes (DR-90), and the key metering is
#                     covered (decision 42).
#   PriorityQueue     P5b (20 headlines): the level order with the
#                     unprioritized level last, FIFO levels and lanes, the
#                     older head first (decision 38), the settle with the
#                     oldest fireable head first and its one fire count, the
#                     re-entry at the FIFO place of a level (decision 43),
#                     the peek restore (Rule E), the priority domain, no
#                     storage for each level (I-10), and the level-scan
#                     metering (decision 42). RecordEnvelope.v adds the
#                     priority and policy slots (2 headlines).
#   JoinCascade       P5c (17 headlines): the joins of one space (decision
#                     29). The greedy search with one guard check (decision
#                     37), the incoming datum bound once (decision 28), the
#                     heads of each head-only collection (decision 11),
#                     distinct records and classes, the retired set
#                     classes, the cascade that ends and restores INV_head
#                     on the head-only disciplines and the set (decision 50)
#                     and INV_scan on the bag, one fire count (decision 49),
#                     lift and re-offer, the bumps of the touched counters,
#                     the bind order of the join slots, plan then lock, the
#                     re-issued orders (decision 43), the second sends of
#                     Rule E (decision 45), and the greedy limit.
#                     RecordEnvelope.v adds continuation_v2_roundtrip, and
#                     CounterConflict.v adds join_ops_race_on_every_counter.
#   TheoryAdmission   P7 step 4 (6 headlines): the theory seam. The builtin
#                     theories decide by shape with one reserved unit, an
#                     admission fails closed at the first value that is not
#                     Proven and a commit refuses two leases, a cache of
#                     checks is transparent, the resolution is a function
#                     of the content of the identity, replay of the
#                     persisted bytes admits as play does, and the bytes of
#                     an identity (decision 74) decode exactly to it.
#                     Match.v adds the TH-6 headline (a theory refusal at a
#                     match is a guard refusal), and SpaceFactory.v adds
#                     gate 4 (theory_gate_validated, TH-4).
#   Similarity        P6 step 2 (20 headlines): the exact decisions of the
#                     VectorDB family over an ordered commutative ring (the
#                     real numbers included): the squared forms of cosine and
#                     euclidean, the monotone bounds, the kernel laws,
#                     Cauchy-Schwarz and the bounds of cosine, the total
#                     score orders, the embedding of the decisions, the
#                     binary metrics, the selection order with the kappa
#                     tie-break and its negative control, and the Qc and Z
#                     instances that discharge the hypotheses.
#   AgentTranslation  P8 step 3 (6 headlines): the translation of a receive
#                     on a space that a user agent implements. The offsets
#                     of the binds partition the binder positions, the env
#                     keys of the binds are disjoint and cover them, the
#                     body binds the values of the native receive, the
#                     guard of its owner bind equals the native guard, the
#                     matcher replies exactly on a spatial match with a
#                     passing guard, and the codec of a matcher state is
#                     exact.
#   Checkpoint        P10 step S7 (8 headlines, C1 to C8): the checkpoint,
#                     the reset, the soft checkpoint and the replay rig of
#                     the host RSpace, the successor of the legacy
#                     Checkpoint.v. A reset gives back the checkpointed
#                     store with its persistent flags, the checkpoint does
#                     not depend on the order of the records of a key, the
#                     rig accepts exactly the log of play, a reset after
#                     the sweep holds no volatile record, the revert of a
#                     soft checkpoint restores the snapshot, and every root
#                     of the history resets. The premises hold for one
#                     concrete instance (checkpoint_premises_satisfiable).
#
# Each module is standalone and imports only the Rocq standard library. A
# verifier compiles each file alone with `coqc -q -noglob` and no -Q or -R
# flags. Zero Admitted. No Axiom, Parameter, Conjecture or Abort. Section
# variables are parameters of the closed theorems.
#
# Build: make (the Makefile regenerates Makefile.conf from this file).
# Gate: scripts/check-reified-rspaces-proofs.sh (builds in a scratch copy and
# runs the negative controls of scripts/verify-reified/rocq-negative-controls.py).

